%N A400811 Size of Type A palindromes of star triples in the Spectre aperiodic monotile tiling.
%C A400811 The chiral aperiodic Spectre monotile tiling (discovered in 2023) forms hierarchical, fractal macro-structures called clusters of star triples (three Spectre tiles head-on) of five different families, megastars of two types, and palindromes of megastars (see A400812). This sequence gives the number of star triples in successive generations of Type A palindromes.
%C A400811 A Type A palindrome has two major star triples in the center and, on both sides of it, the Type A megastars (A397120) of generations 1, 2, ..., n, in straight and reverse order; hence the name, and hence a(n) = 2*(A397120(1) + ... + A397120(n)).
%C A400811 The fractal growth is governed by the limiting constant 5.674473356937... = 1 + 2*sqrt(6)*cos((1/3)*arccos(sqrt(6)/4)), the largest root of x^3 - 3*x^2 - 15*x - 1 = 0, as for the megastars (A397120, A400810).
%C A400811 The vertex span of the Type A palindrome of generation n (the number of star triples on a longest path through it) is Fibonacci(3*n) = A014445(n) = 2*A001076(n).
%H A400811 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400811/b400811.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..100</a>
%H A400811 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400811/a400811.png">Type A palindrome of generation 4 (332 star triples)</a>
%H A400811 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400811/a400811_1.png">Type A palindrome of generation 4 with a longest path (vertex span 144 = Fibonacci(12))</a>
%H A400811 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A400811/a400811_2.png">All Type A palindromes in the level-6 supertile</a>
%H A400811 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/18421797">Anatomy of the Spectre Tiling</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A400811 David Smith, Joseph Samuel Myers, Craig S. Kaplan, and Chaim Goodman-Strauss, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17743">A chiral aperiodic monotile</a>, arXiv:2305.17743 [math.CO], 2023-2024.
%H A400811 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,15,1).
%F A400811 a(n) = 3*a(n-1) + 15*a(n-2) + a(n-3) for n > 3.
%F A400811 a(n) = a(n-1) + 2*A397120(n) for n > 1.
%F A400811 a(n) = 2*Sum_{k=1..n} A397120(k).
%F A400811 G.f.: 2*x*(1 + 2*x)/(1 - 3*x - 15*x^2 - x^3).
%e A400811 For n = 1, the Type A palindrome consists of the two major star triples of its center: a(1) = 2.
%e A400811 For n = 2, it consists of the previous palindrome a(1) = 2 and two Type A megastars of size A397120(2) = 4, one on each side, giving 2 + 2*4 = 10 star triples.
%e A400811 For n = 3, it consists of a(2) = 10 and two Type A megastars of size A397120(3) = 25, giving 10 + 2*25 = 60 star triples.
%t A400811 LinearRecurrence[{3, 15, 1}, {2, 10, 60}, 23]
%o A400811 (PARI) Vec(2*x*(1 + 2*x)/(1 - 3*x - 15*x^2 - x^3) + O(x^24))
%Y A400811 Cf. A397115 (Family A), A397116 (Family C), A397117 (Family B), A397118 (Family D), A397119 (Family E).
%Y A400811 Cf. A397120 (Type A megastars), A400810 (Type C megastars), A400812 (all star triples), A400822 (star triples in all Type A palindromes), A400824 (number of Type A palindromes).
%Y A400811 Cf. A001076, A014445.
